    rdf:value """the Strongs. I regard it as a mere outbreak of spleen and spite against the success of his new book.
Saturday Jan. 23. 04. The Deanery. Bryn Mawr
We saw Mr. Frick’s collection in the morning. Fine Terburg and Rembrandt and Watts, besides the usual more or less boring Barbizons. Came here - 12-10.15, a long, long journey. Carey met us, most kindly. She is wonderful. The house so splendidly organized. We have deliciously comfortable rooms.
Sunday Jan. 24. 04.
Quiet delicious morning. Walked in the afternoon, called on John and poor Mamie, admired Walter Cope’s fine architecture. Mr. and Mrs. Ely came to dine - he the bridge-maker, etc. of the Pennsylvania Railroad; she, alas, a chatterer. """^^xsd:string ;
    mbdiaries-ontology:index 159 ;
    mbdiaries-ontology:part_of <https://mbdiaries.itatti.harvard.edu/resource/diary/1903-04> .

